      "content": "i know, i know... i've heard the \"help is available\" thing a million times. but it just feels so hollow. like, if the core of who i am was built on something that turned out to be fake, then \"i\" don't even exist anymore. how can you \"rebuild\" when the person you were is gone? there's no one left to save. it feels like the truth has just stripped everything away and left me with nothing to hold onto.",
